<h3>Great Buddha Statue and selected monasteries</h3>
<p>If the road has been kind and the temple visit is complete, continue to the <strong>Great Buddha Statue</strong> and one or two nearby monasteries. Bodhgaya has Buddhist communities from many countries, and each tradition has its own architecture and devotional practices. The aim is to understand something about this international pilgrimage town rather than claim to have visited every monastery.</p>
<p>Our guide will suggest the practical order for the time remaining. Additional locations outside the core sightseeing plan can affect the day and should be agreed in advance. A short lunch can be fitted around the confirmed route.</p>
<h3>Return to Varanasi the same evening</h3>
<p>Start the return journey early enough to allow road buffers. We do not advise booking a fixed late-night train or flight immediately after this excursion without checking the connection risk. Children, elderly guests and travellers who dislike extended vehicle travel may prefer staying in Bodhgaya.</p>
<h2>Can you visit Dungeshwari or Sujata Village on this day?</h2>
<p>Both places have importance in the story of the Buddha's path to enlightenment. <strong>Dungeshwari caves</strong> are linked with his period of austerity, while <strong>Sujata Village</strong> is connected with the traditional offering of milk-rice. They are outside the tight core circuit and require additional travel, and Dungeshwari can involve stairs or uneven walking.</p>
<p>We would not automatically include both on a return day trip. If either is a priority, tell us before booking so that we can assess whether it is realistic, whether an additional charge applies and what would need to be left out elsewhere.</p>
<h2>Day trip versus an overnight: which is better value?</h2>
<p>Cost is not the only difference. The day-trip rate covers a private car and guide without hotel nights, but a large share of the day is spent travelling. A two-night plan gives you an evening at the Mahabodhi complex, a full sightseeing day and a more comfortable onward transfer.</p>
